    "body": "This looks pretty good! However, I came up with a different idea, and am curious what you think. In particular I was motivated by:\r\n\r\n- Making \"hand-off to external software\", which takes many of the same inputs, also benefit\r\n- Making \"non-fetch scheme navigation params\" as aligned as possible with normal \"navigation params\" (including by excluding some things that don't make sense for normal navigation params)\r\n- Noticing that it's a bit arbitrary that we left some stuff, like \"initiator origin\", out of \"navigation params\".\r\n\r\nI noticed that \"hand-off to external software\" is the one taking most of these inputs, in the end. In particular, step 4 of \"load a document\" passes in a bunch of navigation params stuff.\r\n\r\nWhat if we did something like the following:\r\n\r\n- Add initiator origin to navigation params.\r\n- Make non-fetch scheme navigation params a true subset of navigation params, consisting of { id, navigation timing type, response, navigable, final sandboxing flag set, initiator origin }.\r\n- Make \"hand-off to external software\" take a URL-or-null, a non-fetch scheme navigation params OR a navigation params, and a boolean hasTransientActivation\r\n- Make \"attempt to create a non-fetch scheme document\" take a URL, a non-fetch scheme navigation params, and a hasTransientActivation boolean\r\n- Then we can update the call sites as follows:\r\n  - \"attempt to create a non-fetch scheme document\" is given entry's URL, the non-fetch scheme navigation params, and sourceSnapshotParams's has transient activation\r\n  - \"hand-off to external software\":\r\n    - inside \"attempt to create a non-fetch scheme document\": pass everything along\r\n    - inside \"load a document\": pass null, navigationParams, and sourceSnapshotParams's has transient activation\r\n  \r\nI'm not sure about this. The URL being sometimes null is awkward. And I'm unclear where to draw the line on what goes in navigation params, and what we decide is too specific to only a few cases and so we leave out. (initiatorOrigin is only used for hand-off to external software, and multipart/x-mixed replace... maybe it's best left out too?)\r\n\r\nBut, I kind of like the subset idea for non-fetch scheme navigation params. In your PR it seems like it's mostly just a bag of parameters used to pass between two algorithms.\r\n\r\nWDYT?",
